# Context: Linux CI job

## Why This Way
All development rounds execute on a Linux machine, but CI had a single
macos-latest job, so a Linux-only regression (CGO behavior, file identity
in internal/watch/fileid.go, path handling) could only surface as a failed
development round. This adds a check-linux job on ubuntu-latest running
make check and make build, per backlog T043 (looper:finding:ci-linux-coverage).

## Gotchas
- No explicit compiler-install step: the ubuntu-latest runner image ships
  gcc and make, which covers CGO.
- make tla deliberately stays macOS-only: TLC is platform-independent
  Java, so a second run doubles runtime and adds no coverage.
- The bench job stays macOS-only: the baseline cache must come from one
  runner type for benchstat comparisons to be meaningful
  (docs/performance.md, "Tracking across commits").

## Verification
- actionlint clean on .github/workflows/ci.yml.
- make check and make build pass on the Linux reference machine (kernel
  6.8), and bin/ohya runs; the actual GitHub-hosted run needs a push and
  is outside this task's authorization.
